{"type":"assistant.message","data":{"messageId":"5cac2d63-c3af-4c4b-bbcd-d2f60d55bba1","content":"Yes, it was worth investigating, and it has been fixed.\n\n### Root Cause\nIn [docs/.vitepress/theme/index.ts](docs/.vitepress/theme/index.ts#L134), the theme configuration specifies `extends: DefaultTheme`. VitePress automatically executes `DefaultTheme.enhanceApp(ctx)` when extending the theme. \n\nHowever, `enhanceApp(ctx)` was also explicitly calling `DefaultTheme.enhanceApp?.(ctx)` inside its body, causing `DefaultTheme.enhanceApp` to run twice on startup. On the second invocation, VitePress attempted to re-register the built-in `Badge` component (`app.component(\"Badge\", VPBadge)`), triggering the Vue runtime warning.\n\n### Fix\nRemoved the redundant `DefaultTheme.enhanceApp?.(ctx)` call in [docs/.vitepress/theme/index.ts](docs/.vitepress/theme/index.ts#L137).","toolRequests":[]},"id":"4f6027ba-94ab-48c2-b433-4fd4ddec0143","timestamp":"2026-09-11T20:56:44.347Z","parentId":"301b2147-34aa-4a66-b2ba-54f2f3be2502"}
